I’ve also checked the proof-level accounting behind the compact witness: \(H_t\) has \(6t-3\) vertices, \(G'\) has \(7t-3\), Proposition 2.1 gives \(\mathrm{gp}_t(H_t)=4t\), and the 22-partite planted graph has clique number exactly 22. Thus Theorem 2.2 makes the expanded certificate an optimum of size \(4t+22\), not merely a feasible set.
