 ## Caveats
 
-- The external oracle gate is not complete: all three arms have zero usable attempts because the supplied OpenRouter key hit its total limit. Do not submit or emit this family as hardened until those runs succeed.
-- Theorem 2.2 is a worst-case result. It does not prove this planted regular distribution hard. A stronger clique, SAT, ILP, SDP, or higher-degree spectral implementation could break it; only the five reported attacks were run.
-- `P(guess)=0/200,000` concerns uniform assignments with exactly one listed vertex per color. It rules out naive structure-aware guessing at the measured resolution, not an informed posterior exploiting hidden motifs.
-- Pair regularity removes degree leakage, but the finite two-switch chain is not proved to sample uniformly from all conditioned regular bipartite graphs. A construction-specific statistic beyond triangle participation may remain.
-- `canonical_key` is a relabelling invariant, not a complete graph-isomorphism canonical form. Nonisomorphic adversarial inputs can share all recorded common-neighbor spectra and four-cycle counts.
-- `H_t` is rendered by the paper's exact symbolic recipe instead of listing thousands of routine edges. Verification uses the resulting clique implication directly; it does not materialize all `7t-3` vertices.
+- External validation is blocked: the supplied OpenRouter key has no remaining quota. Do not submit or emit this family as hardened until the three harness runs have usable attempts.
+- Track B explicitly concedes an efficient solver. The 0.616-second reference time is not a structural-hardness claim; the benchmark measures whether a no-tool solver discovers the 199-operation compression.
+- `P(guess)=0/200,000` samples uniformly from assignments with exactly one vertex per colour. The exact density is `3 / 200003^22`; neither number rules out a structure-aware solver.
+- The four failing attacks were equal-degree selection, zero-first greedy propagation, 64 random restarts, and a common-coordinate ansatz. A full spectral/SDP treatment of the enormous implicit graph was not run. The successful reference scan and the intended cocycle algorithm are reported separately, as Track B requires.
+- `canonical_key` is an invariant under colour permutation, field translation, relation reordering, and their composition, not a complete graph-isomorphism canonical form. Adversarial nonisomorphic instances can collide.
+- `H_t` is given by the paper's exact symbolic recipe rather than millions of explicit edges. Verification checks that `A ∪ B` plus the submitted vertices is a clique; it does not materialize all of `G'`.
+- The earlier random-regular Track A prototype is retained as `rejected_gen_2005_08095_random_regular.py`. It was not shipped because reduction recognition still left the solver with the same large clique search, so its claimed post-insight operation count was not honest.
