codex
One construction audit caught a real issue before finalization: I had placed the three affine roots in the upper eighth of the field to make the baseline scan longer. That violates the same-distribution rule by creating positional bias. I’m removing it and sampling roots uniformly; the expected mechanical scan remains roughly a quarter of a 200,003-element field—still millions of exact operations—without making the planted coordinates statistically special.
apply patch
patch: completed
