+"""Verified generator based on Theorem 2.2 of arXiv:2005.08095.
+
+The paper reduces Maximum Clique to General d-Position by adjoining H_t.
+Here G is a compact, k-partite graph over a prime field.  Every ordinary
+colour-pair relation is the union of three translations.  One exceptional
+pair is the union of three affine maps.  A planted system of translations is
+sampled before the graph is built, so a transversal clique is known without
+solving the generated instance.
+
+The family is Track B.  Lexicographic CSP search must scan most field values,
+while a short additive-cocycle calculation recovers the relative translations
+and turns the exceptional affine relation into the answer.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import hashlib
+import itertools
+import json
+import math
