codex
The first hinted run exposed a harness-detail mismatch: after its one named rung was solved, `harden.py` followed `escalate()` into a second rung. I stopped that scratch-only run and am restarting the diagnostic with `ORACLE_MAX_ESCALATIONS=0`, so its transcript contains exactly the three shipping-preset attempts required by G9.
exec
/bin/bash -lc 'ORACLE_MAX_ESCALATIONS=0 GV_HINT_MODE=structural python3 ../../../scripts/harden.py gen_2005_08095.py' in /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.08095/g9_hinted
