codex
Implemented and locally verified a Track B generator based on the paper’s Theorem 2.2 Maximum-Clique reduction. The mechanical route averages 1,875,091 operations; the cocycle shortcut uses 199.

Key files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.08095/gen_2005_08095.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.08095/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.08095/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.08095/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.08095/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.08095/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass, including 0/200,000 random-guess hits, four attacks at 0/8, exact demo enumeration, scaling, and 80 canonical-key transformations.

The family is parked, not shipped: the bare oracle loop returned `budget_bound`. Every rung through \(p=16{,}000{,}289\) was solved by at least one oracle, while escalation could continue with the same 22-atom answer. The hinted arm was solved 3/3; the placebo arm was unscored because the key reached its quota. No `REJECTED.md` was created, as required for a budget-bound result.

The earlier flawed Track A prototype was preserved as [rejected_gen_2005_08095_random_regular.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.08095/rejected_gen_2005_08095_random_regular.py). The mathematical basis was checked against the [full arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.08095).
